From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
Date: Fri, 05 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] toolhead: backport upstream LOOKAHEAD_FLUSH_TIME 0.250 -> 0.150

Backport of upstream Klipper commit 16fc46fe5 ("toolhead: Reduce
LOOKAHEAD_FLUSH_TIME to 0.150 seconds", Kevin O'Connor, 2025-09-30).

Upstream rationale (from the commit message):
    The current code is likely to perform a lazy flush of the lookahead
    queue around 4 times a second.  Increase that to around 6-7 times a
    second.  This change may slightly improve the responsiveness to user
    requests mid-print (eg, changing extrusion ratio) and may make a
    "print stall" less likely in some corner cases.

Forge-x has independently been shipping the same value on AD5M/AD5M-Pro
units (.shell/commands/ztune_klipper.sh `fix_enable_e17`) as a
workaround for the E0017 "Move Queue Overflow" error — which is one of
the "print stall corner cases" Kevin's commit message refers to.  So
this single value is supported both by an upstream maintainer change
and by months of forge-x field deployment on this exact hardware
class.

We carry it as a patch (not by waiting to move the klipper pin forward
from v0.11.0) because the v0.11 pin is intentional — it matches the
AD5M v11 MCU firmware era and avoids the host<->MCU protocol-skew
risk documented in docs/reverse-engineering/ad5m-mcu-firmware-and-config.md.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@flashforge>
---
 klippy/toolhead.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/klippy/toolhead.py b/klippy/toolhead.py
--- a/klippy/toolhead.py
+++ b/klippy/toolhead.py
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@
         self.cruise_t = cruise_d / cruise_v
         self.decel_t = decel_d / ((end_v + cruise_v) * 0.5)
 
-LOOKAHEAD_FLUSH_TIME = 0.250
+LOOKAHEAD_FLUSH_TIME = 0.150
 
 # Class to track a list of pending move requests and to facilitate
 # "look-ahead" across moves to reduce acceleration between moves.
-- 
2.47.0
